--- !u!114 &1753929911
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1753929908}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8d5be57ef61e14ff39321ed63a581266, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: AudioFeatureLab::AudioFeatureLab.DemoOverlay
  title: Crossfades, FFT, and music
  body: 'Keys 1 through 9 crossfade Music A into Music B. 1 is A, 9 is B. Both stay
    playing. The law is equal-power, so the middle is not twice as loud.

    Select
    Source Crossfader and read blend, sourceAGain, and sourceBGain.


    Z toggles
    the ambience stem. X toggles the drone. SharedTransport gives every scheduled
    source the same DSP start, and SyncedStemPlayer uses PlayScheduled.

    Comma
    fades the pad out. Period fades it back in. That is AudioFader on one source,
    separate from the crossfade.


    The bars analyze the listener mix through
    ListenerSpectrumTap and OnAudioFilterRead, so they follow what you hear, including
    the crossfade.

    Select Listener Tap on the camera for the output peak. Select
    Band Analyzer to edit ranges. Each band''s level is a public float.

    Music
    Clock counts quarter notes at 120 BPM from that same DSP start. pulse peaks on
    each beat.

    Space plays a pooled one-shot.


    M menu. P pauses every voice
    (AudioListener.pause). [ and ] change AudioListener.volume.

    Click the Game
    view so the editor does not take the keys.'
  scroll: {x: 0, y: 0}
  width: 520
